WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.890
Week 4: Identity, Origin, Numbers, and Time. state origin and profession exchange contact numbers tell dates and times

2
00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:32.705
Read for the situation. El formulario pide el nombre, los apellidos y el país de origen. La cita es el martes a las nueve y media. Elena confirma la fecha y guarda el número de contacto. The form asks for the first name, last names, and country of origin. The appointment is Tuesday at nine thirty. Elena confirms the date and saves the contact number.

3
00:00:32.705 --> 00:00:41.595
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:41.595 --> 00:00:46.752
Reading activities. Reading activity 8; Reading activity 9

5
00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:54.938
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:54.938 --> 00:01:16.951
Model language. Soy de los Estados Unidos. — I am from the United States. Mi apellido es Clark. — My last name is Clark. Hoy es el diecinueve de julio. — Today is July nineteenth. Son las tres y cuarto. — It is a quarter past three. ¿A qué hora es la reunión? — What time is the meeting?

7
00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:26.955
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
